WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.833
Accurate documentation can still fail the moment a reader leaves the happy path.

2
00:00:04.833 --> 00:00:10.593
So my test for documentation best practices is whether a reader can finish one task,

3
00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:11.513
see it worked,

4
00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:13.933
and recover from the likeliest failure.

5
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:16.013
That starts with a visible result,

6
00:00:16.013 --> 00:00:19.667
like the error response FastAPI's guide opens with.

7
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.927
Then I'd put recovery beside the risky action,

8
00:00:22.927 --> 00:00:27.467
so after a timeout the reader sees whether a retry is safe.

9
00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:28.387
For a limit,

10
00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:30.707
I'd name a signal the client can inspect,

11
00:00:30.707 --> 00:00:33.600
like GitHub's x-ratelimit-remaining header.

12
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.160
So download the article's review card,

13
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.620
run it on your riskiest page first,

14
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.700
and turn each blank cell into the next change.
